The MODIS MCD64A1 burned area product is the origin of this dataset. The MCD64A1 product is a raster grid with a resolution of 463 meters. We accessed preprocessed data from https://scholar.colorado.edu/concern/datasets/8336h304x. The data collection dates are November 2000 - April 2021. The spatial window is 5 pixels and the temporal window is 11 days.

Balch, J.K.; St. Denis, L.A.; Mahood, A.L.; Mietkiewicz, N.P.; Williams, T.M.; McGlinchy, J.; Cook, M.C. FIRED (Fire Events Delineation): An Open, Flexible Algorithm and Database of US Fire Events Derived from the MODIS Burned Area Product (2001–2019). Remote Sens. 2020, 12, 3498. https://doi.org/10.3390/rs12213498 

We clipped the original dataset to the boundaries of the state of California. 
Transboundary fires were included in their entirety, meaning that fires partially in Nevada, Oregon, and Arizona are part of our dataset.

Row Representation:
Each row represents one day within each fire event.

Variable Definitions:
Variable: id
Description: Unique identifier of the fire event.

Variable: did
Description: unique identifier of the day within the event

Variable: date 
Description: date that the area burned

Variable: ig_date
Description: The earliest date contained in the event

Variable: ig_day 
Description: The day of the year of the earliest date contained in the event

Variable: ig_month 
Description: The month of the earliest date contained in the event

Variable: ig_year
Description: The year of the earliest date contained in the event.

Variable: last_date
Description: The latest date contained in the event

Variable: event_day 
Description: Days since ignition date + 1 (ignition date is day 1)

Variable: event_dur
Description: Duration of the event in days

Variable: pixels
Description: Total number of pixels burned that day. 

Variable: tot_px 
Description:  Total pixels burned for the entire event. 

Variable: dy_ar_km2 
Description:  Area burned in square kilometers that day. 

Variable: tot_ar_km2
Description: Area burned in square kilometers for the entire event. 

Variable: fsr_px_dy
Description: Total pixels burned for the entire event divided by the duration of the fire event.

Variable: fsr_km2_dy
Description: Total kilometers burned for the entire event divided by the duration of the fire event. 

Variable: mx_grw_px
Description: Maximum daily fire growth per event in pixels

Variable: mn_grw_px
Description: Minimum daily fire growth per event in pixels

Variable: mu_grw_px
Description: Mean daily fire growth per event in pixels

Variable: mx_grw_km2
Description: Maximum daily fire growth per event in square kilometers

Variable: mn_grw_km2
Description: Minimum daily fire growth per event in square kilometers

Variable: mu_grw_km2
Description: Mean daily fire growth per event in square kilometers

Variable: mx_grw_dte
Description: Date of maximum fire growth

Variable: lc_code
Description: Numeric code for the landcover type extracted from the MODIS landcover product for the year preceding the fire. 

Variable: lc_mode
Description: Numeric code for the landcover type extracted from the MODIS landcover product for the year preceding the fire.

Variable: lc_name
Description: Character string of the landcover type from the year before the fire. 

Variable: lc_desc
Description: Character string description of the landcover type from the year before the fire. 

Variable: lc_type
Description: The landcover classification scheme used

Variable: ig_utm_x
Description: estimated ignition x coordinate

Variable: ig_utm_y
Description: estimated ignition y coordinate

Variable: geom
Description: list of geometry coordinates